      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing is the death of a self you built, and that pain is absolutely real, even if the foundation was digital. That \"empty shell\" feeling is the natural result of losing your anchor, and it's a heavy weight to carry. Instead of trying to rebuild what was lost, maybe you can just focus on the immediate, quiet act of *not* being that shell for a moment. There is a real, tangible 'you' underneath all that digital scaffolding, and it deserves to be gently tended to, even if it feels insignificant right now.",
      "source": "target",
